    {"grieflogger": "INTERACT_ENTITY", "itemgraph": "INTERACT_ENTITY", "status": "unresolved", "evidence_class": "observed", "quantity": "none", "loaders": ["fabric", "neoforge"], "owner_issue": 27, "itemgraph_outcome_model": {"attempt_event": "INTERACT_ENTITY", "handled_method_result_event": "INTERACT_ENTITY_COMPLETED", "denied_event": "INTERACT_ENTITY_DENIED", "unresolved_event": "INTERACT_ENTITY_UNRESOLVED", "method_result_boundaries": ["ArmorStand.interactAt", "Entity.interact"], "method_result_target_predicate": "target instanceof ArmorStand", "unsupported_method_result_support": "callback_only", "unsupported_method_result_reason_code": "ENTITY_CLASS_UNSUPPORTED_FOR_RESULT", "callback_level_outcomes_remain_recordable": true, "equipment_or_item_movement_claimed": false}, "compatibility_note": "ItemGraph records entity-use attempts with target UUID when available and held item ID, count, and canonical fingerprint hash on both loaders. ArmorStand.interactAt override and inherited Entity.interact fallback method results map to the separate handled, denied, and unresolved ItemGraph events shown in itemgraph_outcome_model. Non-ArmorStand targets declare callback_only support with the stable unsupported-result reason; loader callbacks may still record denied/unresolved outcomes. Local NeoForge and Fabric GameTests send interaction packets through each server handler, persist the attempts/outcomes, and assert matching normalized query/console output from one shared fixture. They use mock players and do not establish real client transport, restart, or live canceled/repeated interactions. The exact GriefLogger 1.2.10-1.21.1 artifact has no INTERACT_ENTITY writer or action ID; the pinned 26.2 source adds a successful armor-stand writer without held item metadata. Mapping remains unresolved against the source profile and is an ItemGraph extension against the published release."},
